Write the current document content on Save As

save_as only copies the document as it already is on disk. An untitled
doc is written by save_file when its content changes, so a doc that was
never edited - or one whose card is still open in the editor - was
copied out as an empty file.

Add a SaveRequested incoming message the desktop wrapper sends after
save_as. It runs localSaveDo, which folds the in-progress editing field
into the tree before serializing, so the new path gets the document as
it currently stands.

